.TITLE "brew"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
The missing package manager for macOS. It installs the __packages__ you need that Apple did not include by default. It manages __binaries__, __libraries__, and __applications__ within their own sandboxed directories.

.DIV "TLDR"
**brew install formula**
Installs a specific package or formula.
> __install__ installation command | __formula__ name of the package

**brew uninstall formula**
Removes an installed formula from the system.
> __uninstall__ removal command | __formula__ name of the package

**brew update**
Fetches the newest version of Homebrew and all formulae from GitHub.
> __update__ sync command

**brew upgrade**
Installs newer versions of all currently installed packages.
> __upgrade__ version update command

**brew list**
Lists all the formulae that are currently installed on the system.
> __list__ display command

**brew doctor**
Checks your system for potential issues and provides suggestions for fixes.
> __doctor__ diagnostic command

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Regularly running __brew cleanup__ is a good habit to remove old versions of installed formulae and free up disk space. Always run __brew doctor__ if you encounter unexpected errors during installation.

